The attached image demonstrates that Nano-11 improves antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and increases antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that OVA-positive migratory dendritic cells (MigDC) in the draining lymph node express high levels of CD86, a costimulatory molecule. Panel B further characterizes OVA-positive and OVA-negative MigDCs based on CD11b and Ly6C expression, indicating that Nano-11 preferentially targets CD11b+ DCs and MoDCs. Panel C, utilizing in vivo imaging, illustrates that Nano-11 (OVA+N11) and aluminum hydroxide (OVA+AH) significantly prolong antigen retention at the injection site compared to soluble OVA alone, which clears rapidly.